  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>As equal &amp; similar charge particle will repel each other, hence will never precipitate. So, the option D is correct.</p><p>Mixing two oppositely charged sols in equal amount neutralises charges and as a result colloids precipitate.</p><p>Only a certain&nbsp;amount of dispersed phase can be added to emulsion without destabilising it.</p><p>Brownian motion stabilises sols.</p>",
